\f1\b\fs36 \cf0 The origins of Astarte\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\fs28 \cf0 1. Her deepest roots: the Semitic Bronze Age world\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Astarte emerges in the 
\f1\b West Semitic religious world
\f0\b0  of the Levant (modern Syria, Lebanon, Israel/Palestine), during the 
\f1\b early\'96middle Bronze Age
\f0\b0  (roughly 
\f1\b 3rd\'962nd millennium BCE
\f0\b0 ).\
She is 
\f1\b not \'93invented\'94 at Ugarit
\f0\b0  \'97 Ugarit is simply where we have the 
\f2\i best preserved texts
\f0\i0 . By the time those texts were written, Astarte was already old, established, and widely known.\
Her name appears in related forms across Semitic languages:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \uc0\u703 A\'9atart
\f0\b0  (Ugaritic / Northwest Semitic)\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \uc0\u703 A\'9at\u333 ret
\f0\b0  (Hebrew, later polemical form)\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ashtart / Astarte
\f0\b0  (Phoenician, Greek rendering)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 This tells us she belonged to a 
\f1\b shared cultural-religious system
\f0\b0 , not a single city cult.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 2. What kind of goddess was she at the beginning?\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Early Astarte was a 
\f1\b multi-functional power goddess
\f0\b0 , not a soft or narrowly defined figure.\
In her oldest form, she combined:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Sexuality & fertility
\f0\b0  (life-force, reproduction, attraction)\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Warfare & violence
\f0\b0  (armed, dangerous, royal power)\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Sovereignty
\f0\b0  (linked to kingship and divine authority)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 This combination might feel contradictory today \'97 but in the Bronze Age, 
\f1\b sex, war, and rulership were all expressions of raw power
\f0\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 3. Relationship to older goddesses (Ishtar connection)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Astarte did not appear out of nowhere. She belongs to a 
\f1\b goddess family tree
\f0\b0 .\
She is closely related to:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Ishtar
\f0\b0  (Mesopotamia)\
\ls3\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Inanna
\f0\b0  (earlier Sumerian form)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 They are 
\f2\i not identical
\f0\i0 , but they overlap strongly:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Love + war\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Venus imagery\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Dangerous sexuality\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Association with kings and battle\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Think of it like this:\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b \cf0 Ishtar/Inanna
\f0\b0  = eastern Mesopotamian branch\uc0\u8232 
\f1\b Astarte
\f0\b0  = western Levantine branch\
They grew out of the same religious soil but evolved locally.\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 4. Astarte at Ugarit: already ancient\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 By the time of 
\f1\b Ugarit
\f0\b0  (14th\'9613th c. BCE), Astarte is already a 
\f1\b recognized divine figure
\f0\b0 , not a newcomer.\
In Ugaritic texts:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 She appears alongside 
\f1\b Baal
\f0\b0 \
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 She is often paired or compared with 
\f1\b Anat
\f0\b0 \
\ls5\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 She acts as a 
\f1\b divine warrior, protector, and political agent
\f0\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 Importantly:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Anat tends to be 
\f2\i purely violent
\f0\i0 \
\ls6\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Astarte blends 
\f1\b violence + erotic power
\f0\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 This tells us that 
\f1\b Astarte\'92s role was already clearly defined
\f0\b0  \'97 she wasn\'92t still \'93forming.\'94\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 5. Why her name matters\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Her name likely comes from a Semitic root related to 
\f1\b radiance or prominence
\f0\b0 , probably connected to the planet 
\f1\b Venus
\f0\b0 (the brightest object in the sky after the sun and moon).\
Venus explains a lot:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Appears at dawn and dusk \uc0\u8594  liminal power\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Associated with desire and danger\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Moves differently from other stars \uc0\u8594  divine agency\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 So from the beginning, Astarte was tied to:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Cosmic cycles
\f0\b0 \
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Sexual magnetism
\f0\b0 \
\ls8\ilvl0
\f1\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Violence and kingship
\f0\b0 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 6. The \'93beginning\'94 of Astarte, summarized\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 There is no single creation myth where Astarte is born.\
Instead, her beginning looks like this:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls9\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \uc0\u55356 \u57101  Emerges gradually in 
\f1\b early Semitic religion
\f0\b0 \
\ls9\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \uc0\u55357 \u56613  Embodies 
\f1\b life, sex, war, and authority
\f0\b0 \
\ls9\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \uc0\u55357 \u56401  Serves as a 
\f1\b power goddess
\f0\b0  for cities and kings\
\ls9\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \uc0\u11088  Linked to 
\f1\b Venus
\f0\b0  and liminal cosmic force\
\ls9\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 \uc0\u55357 \u56826 \u65039  Spreads across the Levant before written records survive\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 By the time writing catches up, 
\f1\b Astarte is already ancient
\f0\b0 .\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf3 \strokec3 \
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f1\b\fs28 \cf0 \strokec2 One last key idea (this matters a lot)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs24 \cf0 Later cultures tried to 
\f1\b tame or moralize her
\f0\b0 :\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls10\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Greeks softened her into Aphrodite\
\ls10\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Biblical writers demonized her\
\ls10\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Romans aestheticized her\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 But her 
\f1\b original form
\f0\b0  is raw, dangerous, and sovereign.\
If you want, next we can:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls11\ilvl0\cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Track how Astarte turns into Aphrodite\
\ls11\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Compare her directly with Anat or Ishtar\
\ls11\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Explain why the Bible treats her as a threat\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
